<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Privacy manifest for the App target. Required since 2024.

  @capacitor/ios ships one for the Capacitor framework itself, but that covers
  the framework, not this app, and none of the four plugins (filesystem, haptics,
  share, cordova-plugin-purchase) ship one at all. Without this file the first
  upload comes back with an ITMS-91053 "Missing API declaration" warning.

  The collection arrays are empty and that is the truth, not an omission: the app
  has no network code, no analytics and no account. The store privacy label is
  "Data Not Collected" on both platforms for the same reason.

  UserDefaults is declared because Capacitor's runtime and the WKWebView's local
  storage both reach it, and it is a "required reason" API. CA92.1 is the reason
  code for reading and writing only this app's own defaults — which is all that
  happens; nothing here touches another app's or a group container's.

  If Apple's post-upload email names an API this file does not declare, add it
  here rather than guessing ahead of time — that email is the authority.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
